        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Familial infantile bilateral striatal necrosis is the familial form of infantile bilateral striatal necrosis (IBSN), a syndrome of bilateral symmetric spongy degeneration of the caudate nucleus, putamen and globus pallidus characterized by developmental regression, choreoathetosis and dystonia progressing to spastic quadriparesis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
