            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A rare familial cardiomyopathy characterized by left ventricular enlargement and/or reduced systolic function preceded or accompanied by significant conduction system disease and/or arrhythmias including bradyarrhythmias, supraventricular or ventricular arrhythmias. Disease onset is usually in early to mid-adulthood. Sudden cardiac death may occur and may be the presenting symptom. In some cases, it is associated with skeletal myopathy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Familial dilated cardiomyopathy with conduction defect due to LMNA mutation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>Familial dilated cardiomyopathy with conduction defect due to LMNA mutation</rdfs:label>
        <skos:broadMatch>ICD-10:I42.0</skos:broadMatch>
        <skos:broadMatch>ICD-11:BC43.00</skos:broadMatch>
        <skos:exactMatch>MONDO:0007269</skos:exactMatch>
