        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Propionic acidemia (PA) is an organic aciduria caused by the deficient activity of the propionyl Coenzyme A carboxylase and is characterized by life threatening episodes of metabolic decompensation, neurological dysfunction and that may be complicated by cardiomyopathy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
