            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A rare, genetic male infertility due to a sperm disorder characterized by the absence of a measurable amount of spermatozoa in the ejaculate (azoospermia), or a number of sperm in the ejaculate inferior to 15 million/mL (oligozoospermia), resulting from a mutation in a single gene known to cause azoo- or oligo-spermia. Sperm morphology may be normal.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Male infertility with azoospermia or oligozoospermia due to single gene mutation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>Male infertility with azoospermia or oligozoospermia due to single gene mutation</rdfs:label>
