        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A disorder of glyoxylate metabolism characterized by an excess of oxalate resulting in kidney stones, nephrocalcinosis and ultimately renal failure and systemic oxalosis. There are 3 types of PH, types 1-3, all caused by liver-specific enzyme defects.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Primary hyperoxaluria</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
