        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Jeune syndrome, also called asphyxiating thoracic dystrophy, is a short-rib dysplasia characterized by a narrow thorax, short limbs and radiological skeletal abnormalities including &apos;trident&apos; aspect of the acetabula and metaphyseal changes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
