        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Intrahepatic cholestasis of pregnancy (ICP) is a cholestatic disorder characterized by (i) pruritus with onset in the second or third trimester of pregnancy, (ii) elevated serum aminotransferases and bile acid levels, and (iii) spontaneous relief of signs and symptoms within two to three weeks after delivery.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">Gravidic intrahepatic cholestasis</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Intrahepatic cholestasis of pregnancy</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
