        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Folinic acid-responsive seizures is a very rare neonatal epileptic encephalopathy disorder characterized clinically by myoclonic and clonic, or clonic seizures associated with apnea occurring several hours to 5 days after birth and responding to folinic acid.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Folinic acid-responsive seizures</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>Folinic acid-responsive seizures</rdfs:label>
