        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Sialidosis type 1 (ST-1) is a very rare lysosomal storage disease, and is the normosomatic form of sialidosis, characterized by gait abnormalities, progressive visual loss, bilateral macular cherry red spots and myoclonic epilepsy and ataxia, that usually presents in the second to third decade of life.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">Cherry-red spot-myoclonus syndrome</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">Lipomucopolysaccharidosis</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">Normomorphic sialidosis</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
