        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A subgroup of porphyria characterized by the occurrence of neurovisceral attacks with or without cutaneous signs. They encompass four diseases: acute intermittent porphyria (PAI; the most common), variegate porphyria (VP), hereditary coproporphyria (HC), and hereditary delta-aminolevulinic acid dehydratase deficiency (ADP; extremely rare).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Acute hepatic porphyria</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>Acute hepatic porphyria</rdfs:label>
