        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Permanent neonatal diabetes mellitus (PNDM) is a monogenic form of neonatal diabetes (NDM) characterized by persistent hyperglycemia within the first 12 months of life in general, requiring continuous insulin treatment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
